    "description": "A treasury service keeps multi-currency account balances for 14 currencies. Amounts arrive as raw BigDecimal together with a currency code string, and every call site decides for itself how to round, whether to allow negative balances and how to compare two amounts. Two production incidents traced back to a debit applied in the wrong currency after a missed null check, and a rounding rule changed in one module without the others following. The accounting team requires that an amount can never exist without its currency, that arithmetic between different currencies is a compile-time or construction-time error rather than a runtime surprise, and that the rounding policy lives in exactly one place. The decision to implement: how to represent the amount-plus-currency pair so illegal combinations cannot be constructed and all arithmetic in the ledger goes through one authoritative representation.",
    "decision_statement": "Represent an amount together with its currency as one self-validating concept whose operations reject invalid combinations.",
    "notes": "Holds when a reviewer replaces kotlin: type-object appears for the rounding-policy axis."
  },
